<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Themed-icon (Android 13+) monochrome layer. The system keeps only the
     alpha channel and paints it in the wallpaper's colour, so the full mark's
     meaning has to survive with one colour and no gradients.

     The colour mark says "dark road on a gold shield"; a single tint cannot
     say dark-on-gold, so this redraws the same geometry as line art:
       · the shield as an outline over a faint (18%) body,
       · the road solid, with the lane dashes cut OUT of it (evenOdd), which is
         what keeps the A readable,
       · the two signal arcs as strokes and the signal dot solid.
     In the colour mark the dot is ringed in dark ink to lift it off the
     road's apex. There is no dark ink here, so at this size the dot and apex
     read as one rounded tip. That is a deliberate simplification, not a
     rendering fault.

     Same 128-unit coordinates and the same 0.6 safe-zone scale as
     ic_logo_fg.xml, so the themed and colour icons sit in the same place. -->
